.TH wall-c 1 "February 2026" "wall-c 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wall-c \- send Wake-on-LAN magic packets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wall-c
[\-m MAC]
[\-\-target NAME]
[\-b IP]
[\-\-interface IFACE]
[\-p PORT]
[\-\-count N]
[\-\-interval-ms MS]
[\-\-dry-run]
[\-\-continue-on-error]
[\-\-quiet]
[\-y]
[\-h]
[\-\-version]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBwall-c\fR sends Wake-on-LAN (WoL) magic packets over UDP broadcast.
Targets can come from command line, stdin, or config file entries.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-mac MAC
Target MAC address.
Accepted forms: XX:XX:XX:XX:XX:XX, XX-XX-XX-XX-XX-XX, XXXXXXXXXXXX.
.TP
.B \-\-target NAME
Select one named target from the config file.
.TP
.B \-\-list-targets
Print parsed targets from config and exit.
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-broadcast IP
Broadcast IPv4 address (default: 255.255.255.255).
.TP
.B \-\-interface IFACE
Resolve broadcast IPv4 address from interface name (for example, en0).
Cannot be combined with \-b/\-\-broadcast.
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-port PORT
UDP destination port (default: 9).
.TP
.B \-\-count N
Number of packets to send per target (default: 1).
.TP
.B \-\-interval-ms MS
Delay in milliseconds between repeated sends (default: 0).
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Validate inputs and print actions without sending packets.
.TP
.B \-\-continue-on-error
Continue processing later targets after a failure in batch mode.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Reduce non-error output.
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-yes
Skip interactive confirmation prompt.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.SH TARGET PRECEDENCE
When no explicit source is given, target selection is:
.IP "1." 3
\-m/\-\-mac
.IP "2." 3
\-\-target
.IP "3." 3
First non-empty, non-comment line from stdin
.IP "4." 3
All targets from config file
.SH CONFIG FILE
Path resolution:
.IP "1." 3
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wall-c/config
.IP "2." 3
$HOME/.config/wall-c/config
.PP
Supported line formats:
.IP "1." 3
MAC [BROADCAST_IP] [PORT]
.IP "2." 3
NAME MAC [BROADCAST_IP] [PORT]
.PP
Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Validation, config, or send failure.
